				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-042e685 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="042e685" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>Candidates seeking information on running in City &amp; County of Honolulu races may contact our office. Individuals interested in all other offices may obtain information from the State of Hawaii <strong><a href="https://elections.hawaii.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OFFICE OF ELECTIONS.</a></strong></p><div>Candidate Filing for the 2026 Elections begins February 2, 2026 and ends June 2, 2026.</div><div> </div><p><strong>City &amp; County of Honolulu offices up for election in 2026 are:</strong></p><p><span style="font-style: inherit;font-weight: inherit">Councilmember<br /></span><span style="font-style: inherit;font-weight: inherit">&#8211; District II<br /></span><span style="font-style: inherit;font-weight: inherit">&#8211; District IV<br /></span><span style="font-style: inherit;font-weight: inherit">&#8211; District VI<br /></span><span style="font-style: inherit;font-weight: inherit">&#8211; District VIII</span></p><p>Applications are accepted by appointment only, at Honolulu Hale, 530 South King Street, Room 100, Honolulu, HI 96813. Contact the Office of the City Clerk at (808) 768-3800 to schedule an appointment between Monday to Friday from 7:45 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.</p><p>The Office of the City Clerk <strong>does not</strong> accept filings for Federal and State contests.</p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d25af7e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="d25af7e" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-98550d3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="98550d3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h4 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">FILING FEES (CITY CONTESTS)</h4>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-28f7b62 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="28f7b62" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><strong style="font-style: inherit;text-align: var(--text-align);color: var(--ast-global-color-8);background-color: var(--ast-global-color-1)">Councilmember</strong><span style="font-style: inherit;font-weight: inherit;text-align: var(--text-align);color: var(--ast-global-color-8);background-color: var(--ast-global-color-1)"> &#8211; $250 (Discounted fee $25 with Affidavit to Voluntarily Agree with Campaign Expenditure Limits)</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8e6ac50 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="8e6ac50" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9441dc3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="9441dc3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h4 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">CAMPAIGN SIGN REGULATIONS IN HAWAII</h4>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8c8109c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="8c8109c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>The City Department of Planning and Permitting has issued the following regulations for political-related signs.<br /><strong>&#8211;<a href="https://www.honolulu.gov/elections/wp-content/uploads/sites/60/2026/09/DPP-Regulations-for-Political-Related-Signage.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DPP Regulations for Political-Related Signage</a></strong></p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e03b872 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="e03b872" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2255f7b elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="2255f7b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h4 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">NON-ELECTIONEERING GUIDELINES</h4>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d5c2dbb elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="d5c2dbb" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>On election days, campaign signs and electioneering activities are regulated by <a href="https://www.honolulu.gov/elections/wp-content/uploads/sites/60/2024/04/HRS_0011-0132.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hawaii Revised Statute § 11-132</a> . A 200 foot buffer area from the perimeter of any voter service center, place of deposit, and its  appurtenances must be free of campaign activity.<br />Persons wearing campaign clothing will be asked to cover the item of clothing while in the voter service center or leave the premises.</p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-155a825 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="155a825" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-56fd116 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="56fd116" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h4 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Electioneering Maps for Voter Service Centers and Places of Deposit Locations</h4>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-18dfcb2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="18dfcb2" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><a href="https://www.honolulu.gov/elections/wp-content/uploads/sites/60/2024/04/2022_Voter_Service_Center_Electioneering_Maps.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>-Voter Service Center Electioneering Maps</strong></a><br /><a href="https://www.honolulu.gov/elections/wp-content/uploads/sites/60/2024/06/2024-Places-of-Deposit-Electioneering-Map2.0.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>-Places of Deposit Electioneering Maps</strong></a> </p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b8db95d e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="b8db95d" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5374f26 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="5374f26" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h4 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">CANDIDATE FILING LIST (UNCERTIFIED)</h4>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4f2f954 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="4f2f954" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>The <strong><a href="https://elections.hawaii.gov/candidates/candidate-reports/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CANDIDATE REPORT</a>,</strong> a list of candidates that have applied for nomination papers and/or filed for candidacy, will be available from the State of Hawaii Office of Election&#8217;s website.</p>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				</div>
			</div> <!-- ast-container -->
	</div><!-- #content -->
